+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, [
+  { op: "test", path: "/foo/0", value: "bar" },
+  { op: "add", path: "/foo/1", value: "qux" },
+  { op: "move", from: "/foo/0", path: "/first" },
+]); // { foo: ["qux", "baz"], first: "bar" }
+```
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations in
+order and returns the result as a new value; neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure
+with them. It throws a `JsonPatchError` if the patch is malformed (not an array, unknown `op`, missing or
+invalid `path`/`from`/`value`) or if any operation fails (missing target, bad array index, `move` into its own
+child, failed `test`); nothing is returned in that case. `remove` with the empty path (the whole document)
+is rejected. Members named `__proto__` are handled as ordinary data.
+
 Tests: `npm test`.
