+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Lets services update a JSON document with a standard JSON Patch (RFC 6902), producing a new document and failing loudly, without partial results, when the patch is malformed or an operation cannot be applied.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch application is pure and atomic
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` SHALL apply the operations of `patch` in order (RFC 6902 §3, §4) to `document` and return the resulting document. It SHALL NOT mutate `document` or `patch`, and the result SHALL NOT share mutable structure with either. If any operation fails (RFC 6902 §5) it SHALL throw and return nothing.
+
+#### Scenario: Operations apply in order
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":1},{"op":"replace","path":"/a","value":2}]` on `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Inputs are not mutated
+- **WHEN** a patch with several operations is applied to a nested document
+- **THEN** the document and the patch are deeply equal to their state before the call
+
+#### Scenario: Result does not alias inputs
+- **WHEN** a patch adds a `value` that is an object, or the document is returned unchanged by an empty patch
+- **THEN** mutating the result does not change the patch or the original document
+
+#### Scenario: Failure leaves nothing applied
+- **WHEN** the first operation is valid but the second fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** the result is a document deeply equal to the input
+
+### Requirement: Patch structure is validated
+The patch SHALL be an array of operation objects (RFC 6902 §3). Each operation SHALL have a string `op` that is one of the six operation names, and a string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have a `value` member (which may be `null`); `move` and `copy` SHALL have a string `from` that is a valid pointer. Members not defined for the operation SHALL be ignored (§4). Invalid patches SHALL throw, even if earlier operations would succeed.
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, string, `null` or `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Operation is not an object
+- **WHEN** an element is `null`, an array, or a string
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or unknown op
+- **WHEN** an operation has no `op`, a non-string `op`, or `op` is `"increment"` or `"ADD"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid path
+- **WHEN** `path` is absent, not a string, or not a valid pointer such as `"a"` or `"/a~2"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add`, `replace` or `test` operation has no `value` member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown, but `"value": null` is accepted
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid from
+- **WHEN** a `move` or `copy` operation has no `from`, a non-string `from`, or an invalid pointer
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unrelated members are ignored
+- **WHEN** an operation carries an extra member such as `"comment"`, or `from` on an `add`
+- **THEN** the operation applies normally
+
+### Requirement: add operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.1, `add` SHALL, when the target is an object member, set it (replacing any existing value); when the target is an array index, insert before that index, shifting later elements; when the index is `-`, append; and when the path is `""`, replace the whole document. The parent of the target MUST exist, and an array index MUST be a valid index no greater than the array length.
+
+#### Scenario: Add new object member
+- **WHEN** `add` `/c` with value `3` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1,"c":3}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces existing member
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a` with value `2` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `add` `/foo/1` with value `"qux"` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Append with dash and at length
+- **WHEN** `add` `/foo/-` or `/foo/2` with value `"x"` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","baz","x"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Add whole document
+- **WHEN** `add` with path `""` and value `[1]` is applied to any document
+- **THEN** the result is `[1]`
+
+#### Scenario: Missing parent
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/b/c` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Array index out of range or malformed
+- **WHEN** `add` targets `/foo/3` on a 2-element array, `/foo/-1`, `/foo/01` or `/foo/x`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Parent is a scalar
+- **WHEN** `add` `/a/b` is applied to `{"a":1}` or `{"a":null}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: remove operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.2, `remove` SHALL delete the target, which MUST exist. Removing an array element SHALL shift later elements down. Removing the whole document (path `""`) is not supported and SHALL throw.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove object member
+- **WHEN** `remove` `/a` is applied to `{"a":1,"b":2}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":2}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** `remove` `/foo/1` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** `remove` targets a missing member, an out-of-range index, `-`, or a member of a scalar
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Remove root
+- **WHEN** `remove` has path `""`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.3, `replace` SHALL set the value at the target, which MUST exist, equivalent to a `remove` followed by an `add`. With path `""` it SHALL replace the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member and element
+- **WHEN** `replace` `/a` with `2` is applied to `{"a":1}`, or `/foo/0` with `"x"` to `{"foo":["bar"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":2}` or `{"foo":["x"]}` respectively
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** `replace` targets a missing member, index equal to the array length, or `-`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace root
+- **WHEN** `replace` has path `""` and value `{"x":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"x":1}`
+
+### Requirement: move operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.4, `move` SHALL remove the value at `from` (which MUST exist) and add it at `path`, as `remove` then `add`. `from` MUST NOT be a proper prefix of `path` (a location cannot be moved into one of its children).
+
+#### Scenario: Move object member
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a` to `/b` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"b":1}`
+
+#### Scenario: Move array element
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/foo/1` to `/foo/3` is applied to `{"foo":["a","b","c","d"]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"foo":["a","c","d","b"]}` (the add index is evaluated after the removal)
+
+#### Scenario: Move to same location
+- **WHEN** `from` equals `path` and the location exists
+- **THEN** the document is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a` to `/a/b`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move to root
+- **WHEN** `move` from `/a` to `""` is applied to `{"a":{"x":1}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"x":1}` (remove, then add replaces the whole document)
+
+#### Scenario: Move from root
+- **WHEN** `move` has `from` `""` and a non-empty `path`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown (`""` is a proper prefix of `path`)
+
+### Requirement: copy operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.5, `copy` SHALL add a deep copy of the value at `from` (which MUST exist) at `path`, with `add` semantics, leaving `from` in place.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** `copy` from `/a` to `/b` is applied to `{"a":{"x":1}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"x":1},"b":{"x":1}}` and the two values are distinct objects
+
+#### Scenario: Copy into array
+- **WHEN** `copy` from `/a` to `/list/-` is applied to `{"a":1,"list":[]}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":1,"list":[1]}`
+
+#### Scenario: Copy from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Copy into own child
+- **WHEN** `copy` from `/a` to `/a/b` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":{"b":{}}}`
+
+### Requirement: test operation
+Per RFC 6902 §4.6, `test` SHALL succeed only if the value at `path` (which MUST exist) is equal to `value`, and SHALL throw otherwise, which aborts the patch. Equality: same JSON type; strings equal code-unit for code-unit; numbers equal by numeric value (`1` equals `1.0`); arrays equal if same length and elements equal in order; objects equal if same set of member names and equal values, regardless of member order; `null`, `true`, `false` equal only themselves. `test` SHALL NOT change the document.
+
+#### Scenario: Test passes
+- **WHEN** `test` `/a` with value `{"x":[1,2],"y":null}` is applied to `{"a":{"y":null,"x":[1,2]}}`
+- **THEN** the document is returned unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Test fails on value difference
+- **WHEN** the values differ, including array order `[1,2]` vs `[2,1]`, extra or missing object members, or `"1"` vs `1`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Test null vs missing
+- **WHEN** `test` `/a` with value `null` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown, whereas it passes for `{"a":null}`
+
+#### Scenario: Test whole document
+- **WHEN** `test` has path `""`
+- **THEN** the whole document is compared with `value`
+
+#### Scenario: Test aborts the patch
+- **WHEN** a failing `test` precedes an `add`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown (conditional patching, §4.6)
+
+### Requirement: Hostile keys are handled safely
+Documents and patches are untrusted. Members named `__proto__`, `constructor` or `prototype` SHALL be treated as ordinary own data members, SHALL NOT alter any prototype, and inherited properties SHALL NOT be considered to exist.
+
+#### Scenario: Add __proto__ member
+- **WHEN** `add` `/__proto__/polluted` with value `true` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown (no such parent) and `Object.prototype` is unaffected
+
+#### Scenario: Own __proto__ member from JSON
+- **WHEN** a patch parsed from `{"op":"add","path":"/__proto__","value":{"x":1}}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member `__proto__` equal to `{"x":1}`, and `Object.getPrototypeOf(result)` is still `Object.prototype`
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited names are not members
+- **WHEN** `remove`, `replace` or `test` targets `/toString` or `/constructor` on `{}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Cloned values keep own __proto__
+- **WHEN** a document containing an own `__proto__` member is patched
+- **THEN** that member is preserved as own data in the result with the prototype unchanged
