+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Core machinery and validation
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `JsonPatchError`, safe deep clone, §4.6 equality and target-location helpers to `src/index.ts`; verify with `npm test` that `test/patch.test.ts` cases for clone/equality (own `__proto__`, key order, number/string/null types) pass
+- [x] 1.2 Add structural validation of the patch and `applyPatch(document, patch)` skeleton; verify tests for every "Patch structure is validated" scenario and for empty patch, purity, no-aliasing and atomic failure pass with `npm test`
+
+## 2. Operations
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `add`, `remove`, `replace`; verify tests for all scenarios of those three requirements (array insert, `-`, index bounds, leading zeros, missing parent, scalar parent, root cases) pass with `npm test`
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `move`, `copy`; verify tests for all their scenarios (index evaluated after removal, same location, prefix rule, root, deep-copy independence) pass with `npm test`
+- [x] 2.3 Implement `test`; verify tests for all its scenarios (equality rules, null vs missing, root, abort) pass with `npm test`
+- [x] 2.4 Add hostile-key tests (`__proto__`, `constructor`, inherited names) and the RFC 6902 Appendix A examples as tests; verify `npm test` passes and `Object.prototype` is unpolluted
+
+## 3. Documentation and integration
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add a JSON Patch section to `README.md` (usage, errors, `remove ""` behaviour); verify the README example runs as written
+- [x] 3.2 Run the full `npm test` and `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` if TypeScript is available; verify both are clean (`npm test` clean; TypeScript is not installed here, so `tsc` was not run)
